                "word": "sériosité",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "accbf839-651f-3797-9890-87bb7e605967",
                        "entry_id": "c2ed440c-73b9-3a31-b680-5731ede83f28",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Caractère de ce qui est sérieux ; qualité d’une personne ou d’une chose sérieuse."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2e1c1749-ca9e-4d4f-a0e5-8c049ca0fede",
                                "sense_id": "accbf839-651f-3797-9890-87bb7e605967",
                                "text": "Avec la sériosité d’un « Herr Professor » mon amie a répondu qu’en Roumanie tous les gens bien parlaient français !"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "42a6bf7c-3917-3225-9383-6492e0badfa7",
                        "entry_id": "c2ed440c-73b9-3a31-b680-5731ede83f28",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Tendance à tout prendre au sérieux."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1f6e8616-b516-45f3-9053-275634b7f7c8",
                                "sense_id": "42a6bf7c-3917-3225-9383-6492e0badfa7",
                                "text": "Il y a eu des civilisations florissantes, des civilisations de bâtisseurs, des civilisations artistiques ; la civilisation actuelle est sérieuse. Une vague de sériosité la submerge."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b6d2d88e-3d59-4233-b93e-07ea35b31177",
                                "sense_id": "42a6bf7c-3917-3225-9383-6492e0badfa7",
                                "text": "La « sériosité », cette maladie qui consiste à être sérieux tout le temps, est génératrice d’un terrible ennui … »"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d57b7eeb-a5fe-45ba-b0be-273cc49f94a6",
                        "source_entry_id": "c2ed440c-73b9-3a31-b680-5731ede83f28",
                        "target_lang_word": "seriousness",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "seriousness",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f74dbf7c-7fe7-3c3e-812b-4e371b019caa",
                                        "entry_id": "b73c1504-5415-3014-b3fb-c85e200f5d94",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state or quality of being serious."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e4ff3e78-1ce3-4e7b-a15e-4636c725a220",
                                                "sense_id": "f74dbf7c-7fe7-3c3e-812b-4e371b019caa",
                                                "text": "“[…] She takes the whole thing with desperate seriousness. But the others are all easy and jovial—thinking about the good fare that is soon to be eaten, about the hired fly, about anything.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bb9bde4f-7d4a-462a-aca4-173d84fc4119",
                                                "sense_id": "f74dbf7c-7fe7-3c3e-812b-4e371b019caa",
                                                "text": "‘Then the father has a great fight with his terrible conscience,’ said Munday with granite seriousness. ‘Should he make a row with the police […]? Or should he say nothing about it and condone brutality for fear of appearing in the newspapers?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b7527e2a-7822-46c2-be38-7f7e4453d088",
                                                "sense_id": "f74dbf7c-7fe7-3c3e-812b-4e371b019caa",
                                                "text": "Though Bane’s sing-song voice gives his pronouncements a funny lilt, he doesn’t have any of the Joker’s deranged wit, and Nolan isn’t interested in undercutting his seriousness for the sake of a breezier entertainment."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
